        "id": "F1",
        "label": "An error or a lost worker leaves the export running forever",
        "rank": "P2",
        "kind": "Confirmed gap",
        "detail": "run_export has no exception handling and nothing reclaims a claimed row. failed is allowed by the CHECK constraint and never written.",
        "evidence": "app/worker/runner.py run_export; db/schema.sql exports.export_job",
        "invariant": "Every claimed export ends: succeeded, failed or cancelled.",
        "impact": "The export shows running, or Stopping…, with no way out. The open upload is never aborted.",
        "reproduction": "Claim an export, then make render_parts raise or kill the worker. The row keeps state running.",
        "owner": "The worker’s claim: it needs a lease the database can expire.",
        "repair": "Proposal: give the claim a lease_expires_at that the worker renews per part; a sweeper ends expired rows failed and aborts their uploads. Catch render errors and finish failed.",
        "closure": "A test that kills the worker after the claim and asserts the sweeper ends the row failed and aborts the upload.",
        "nodes": [
          "running",
          "stopping",
          "failed"
